    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# `sklearn.covariance`.empirical_covariance¶\n\n- \n`sklearn.covariance.``empirical_covariance` (*X* ,*assume_centered=False* )[source]¶\n- Computes the Maximum likelihood covariance estimator Parameters: **X** : ndarray, shape (n_samples, n_features)Data from which to compute the covariance estimate **assume_centered** : BooleanIf True, data are not centered before computation. Useful when working with data whose mean is almost, but not exactly zero. If False, data are centered before computation. Returns: **covariance** : 2D ndarray, shape (n_features, n_features)Empirical covariance (Maximum Likelihood Estimator).",
    "markdown_length": 620,
